- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7"
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "id": 7,
  "name": "Website",
  "description": "",
  "monitor_type": "http",
  "target": "https://example.com",
  "parent_id": null,
  "interval_seconds": 60,
  "retry_interval_seconds": null,
  "timeout_seconds": 10,
  "retries": 1,
  "active": true,
  "upside_down": false,
  "http_method": "GET",
  "accepted_status_codes": "200-399",
  "max_redirects": 10,
  "ignore_tls": false,
  "expiry_notify": true,
  "expiry_days": 14,
  "status": "up",
  "tags": [{"id": 2, "name": "production", "color": "green", "value": ""}],
  "notifications": [{"channel_id": 1, "escalation": false}],
  "created_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00"
}
```

### PUT /api/v1/monitors/{id}

Replace a monitor: fields you leave out go back to their defaults (tags and notifications are kept unless sent).

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Body: JSON object; fields used in the example: `escalation_minutes` (integer), `interval_seconds` (integer), `monitor_type` (string), `name` (string), `notifications` (array), `retries` (integer), `tags` (array), `target` (string)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X PUT -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7" -d '{
  "name": "Website",
  "monitor_type": "http",
  "target": "https://example.com",
  "interval_seconds": 60,
  "retries": 1,
  "tags": ["production", {"name": "env", "value": "prod"}],
  "notifications": [1, {"channel_id": 3, "escalation": true}],
  "escalation_minutes": 15
}'
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "id": 7,
  "name": "Website",
  "description": "",
  "monitor_type": "http",
  "target": "https://example.com",
  "parent_id": null,
  "interval_seconds": 60,
  "retry_interval_seconds": null,
  "timeout_seconds": 10,
  "retries": 1,
  "active": true,
  "upside_down": false,
  "http_method": "GET",
  "accepted_status_codes": "200-399",
  "max_redirects": 10,
  "ignore_tls": false,
  "expiry_notify": true,
  "expiry_days": 14,
  "status": "up",
  "tags": [{"id": 2, "name": "production", "color": "green", "value": ""}],
  "notifications": [{"channel_id": 1, "escalation": false}],
  "created_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00"
}
```

### PATCH /api/v1/monitors/{id}

Change some fields; everything else stays. Send "••••••" for a secret to keep it.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Body: JSON object; fields used in the example: `interval_seconds` (integer), `retries` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X PATCH -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7" -d '{"interval_seconds": 30, "retries": 2}'
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "id": 7,
  "name": "Website",
  "description": "",
  "monitor_type": "http",
  "target": "https://example.com",
  "parent_id": null,
  "interval_seconds": 60,
  "retry_interval_seconds": null,
  "timeout_seconds": 10,
  "retries": 1,
  "active": true,
  "upside_down": false,
  "http_method": "GET",
  "accepted_status_codes": "200-399",
  "max_redirects": 10,
  "ignore_tls": false,
  "expiry_notify": true,
  "expiry_days": 14,
  "status": "up",
  "tags": [{"id": 2, "name": "production", "color": "green", "value": ""}],
  "notifications": [{"channel_id": 1, "escalation": false}],
  "created_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00"
}
```

### DELETE /api/v1/monitors/{id}

Delete a monitor and its history. Returns 204.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `204 No Content`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X DELETE -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7"
```

