### POST /api/v1/monitors/{id}/check

Run a check right now and return its result (409 for paused, push and group monitors).

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7/check"
```

Example response:

```json
{"status": "up", "heartbeat": {"id": 991, "status": "up", "response_time_ms": 84, "message": "200 OK", "checked_at": "2026-10-19 14:03:00"}}
```

### GET /api/v1/monitors/{id}/heartbeats

Check history, newest first (local checks only).

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Query parameters:
  - `since`: UTC time, e.g. 2026-10-19 00:00:00
  - `limit`: page size (1–500, default 50)
  - `cursor`: next_cursor from the previous page

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7/heartbeats"
```

Example response:

```json
{"data": [{"id": 991, "monitor_id": 7, "agent_id": null, "status": "up", "response_time_ms": 84, "message": "200 OK", "checked_at": "2026-10-19 14:03:00"}], "next_cursor": "940"}
```

### GET /api/v1/monitors/{id}/uptime

Uptime over a window plus one entry per day (survives heartbeat retention).

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Query parameters:
  - `days`: 1–365 (default 30)

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7/uptime"
```

Example response:

```json
{"monitor_id": 7, "days": 30, "uptime_pct": 99.98, "uptime_24h_pct": 100.0, "daily": [{"day": "2026-10-19", "up": 1440, "down": 0, "pending": 0, "maintenance": 0, "avg_ms": 82.4, "uptime_pct": 100.0}]}
```

### GET /api/v1/monitors/{id}/events

Outages, maintenance, pauses and other events, newest first.

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Query parameters:
  - `limit`: page size (1–500, default 50)

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7/events"
```

Example response:

```json
{"data": [{"id": 12, "monitor_id": 7, "kind": "down", "message": "timeout", "started_at": "2026-10-18 03:10:00", "ended_at": "2026-10-18 03:14:00", "duration_seconds": 240}], "next_cursor": null}
```

### PUT /api/v1/monitors/{id}/tags

Replace a monitor's tags (names are created if new).

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Body: JSON array (see the example)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X PUT -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/7/tags" -d '["production", {"name": "env", "value": "prod"}, {"id": 4}]'
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "id": 7,
  "name": "Website",
  "description": "",
  "monitor_type": "http",
  "target": "https://example.com",
  "parent_id": null,
  "interval_seconds": 60,
  "retry_interval_seconds": null,
  "timeout_seconds": 10,
  "retries": 1,
  "active": true,
  "upside_down": false,
  "http_method": "GET",
  "accepted_status_codes": "200-399",
  "max_redirects": 10,
  "ignore_tls": false,
  "expiry_notify": true,
  "expiry_days": 14,
  "status": "up",
  "tags": [{"id": 2, "name": "production", "color": "green", "value": ""}],
  "notifications": [{"channel_id": 1, "escalation": false}],
  "created_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-10-19 08:00:00"
}
```

### POST /api/v1/monitors/bulk

Change settings on many monitors at once (ids, or every monitor matching a filter like the list's). Each setting is optional; it uses the monitor form's validation and one transaction. Settings that don't apply to a monitor's type are skipped and listed: agents_unsupported, timing_unsupported, timeout_exceeds_interval, escalation_needs_delay.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Body: JSON object; fields used in the example: `filter` (object), `set` (object)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/monitors/bulk" -d '{"filter": {"type": "http", "tag": "production"}, "set": {"run_on_agents": true, "confirm_with_agents": true, "interval_seconds": 120, "channels": {"add": [{"name": "Ops Discord", "escalation": false}], "remove": [3]}, "tags": {"add": [{"name": "eu", "color": "teal", "value": "west"}], "remove": ["legacy"]}}}'
```

Example response:

```json
{"updated": 38, "skipped": [{"id": 12, "reason": "agents_unsupported"}]}
```

## Endpoints: Tags

### GET /api/v1/tags

List tags with how many monitors use them.

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/tags"
```

Example response:

```json
{"data": [{"id": 2, "name": "production", "color": "green", "monitors": 12}], "next_cursor": null}
```

### POST /api/v1/tags

Create a tag. Colours are palette names (red, orange, yellow, green, mint, teal, cyan, blue, indigo, purple, pink, brown, gray); hex values map to the nearest.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `201 Created`
- Body: JSON object; fields used in the example: `color` (string), `name` (string)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/tags" -d '{"name": "production", "color": "green"}'
```

Example response:

```json
{"id": 2, "name": "production", "color": "green"}
```

### GET /api/v1/tags/{id}

Get one tag.

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/tags/1"
```

### PATCH /api/v1/tags/{id}

Rename or recolour a tag.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Body: JSON object; fields used in the example: `color` (string)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X PATCH -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/tags/1" -d '{"color": "teal"}'
```

### DELETE /api/v1/tags/{id}

Delete a tag (it is removed from every monitor).

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `204 No Content`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X DELETE -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/tags/1"
```

## Endpoints: Notifications

### GET /api/v1/notification-providers

Every channel kind with its config fields (which are required, which are secret).

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/notification-providers"
```

Example response:

```json
{"data": [{"kind": "discord", "label": "Discord", "fields": [{"key": "url", "type": "url", "required": true, "secret": true}]}]}
```

### GET /api/v1/notification-channels

List channels. Secrets are always masked as "••••••".

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/notification-channels"
```

Example response:

```json
{"data": [{"id": 1, "name": "Ops Discord", "kind": "discord", "active": true, "is_default": true, "monitors": 12, "config": {"url": "••••••", "username": "Vole"}}], "next_cursor": null}
```

### POST /api/v1/notification-channels

Create a channel. apply_existing links it to every monitor.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `201 Created`
- Body: JSON object; fields used in the example: `apply_existing` (boolean), `config` (object), `is_default` (boolean), `kind` (string), `name` (string)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/notification-channels" -d '{"name": "Ops Discord", "kind": "discord", "config": {"url": "https://discord.com/api/webhooks/…"}, "is_default": true, "apply_existing": false}'
```

### GET /api/v1/notification-channels/{id}

Get one channel (secrets masked).

- Access: viewer (any API token, read scope is enough)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/notification-channels/1"
```

### PATCH /api/v1/notification-channels/{id}

Update a channel. Secrets you leave out or send masked keep their stored value.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)
- Body: JSON object; fields used in the example: `active` (boolean)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X PATCH -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" "$VV_URL/api/v1/notification-channels/1" -d '{"active": false}'
```

### DELETE /api/v1/notification-channels/{id}

Delete a channel.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `204 No Content`
- Path parameters: `id` (integer)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X DELETE -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/notification-channels/1"
```

### POST /api/v1/notification-channels/{id}/test

Send a test notification (502 with the provider's error when delivery fails).

