## Endpoints: Configuration

### GET /api/v1/config

Export the whole configuration as YAML or JSON. Secrets are masked unless an admin asks for them.

- Access: editor (write token of an editor or admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Query parameters:
  - `format`: yaml (default) | json
  - `secrets`: 1 to include secrets (admins only)
  - `download`: 1 to download as a file

Example request:

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" "$VV_URL/api/v1/config" -o vigilant.yml
```

Example response:

```yaml
version: 1
tags:
  - name: production
    color: green
notification_channels:
  - name: Ops Discord
    kind: discord
    config:
      url: "••••••"
monitors:
  - name: Website
    monitor_type: http
    target: https://example.com
    interval_seconds: 30
    tags: [production]
    notifications: [Ops Discord]
status_pages:
  - slug: acme
    title: Acme status
    sections:
      - name: Services
        monitors: [Website]
```

### POST /api/v1/config

Import a configuration document (YAML or JSON body). Merge upserts by key; replace also deletes what the document doesn't list in the sections it contains. Masked secrets keep stored values.

- Access: admin (write token of an admin)
- Success: `200 OK`
- Query parameters:
  - `mode`: merge (default) | replace
  - `dry_run`: 1 to only return the plan
  - `confirm`: 1, required to apply a replace
- Body: a configuration document in YAML or JSON (see the example and "Config as code" below)

Example request:

```bash
curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $VV_TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/yaml" --data-binary @vigilant.yml "$VV_URL/api/v1/config?dry_run=1"
```

Example response:

```json
{
  "applied": false,
  "mode": "merge",
  "summary": {"create": 2, "update": 1, "delete": 0, "unchanged": 14, "skip": 0},
  "items": [
    {"kind": "monitor", "key": "Website", "action": "update", "changes": ["interval_seconds"]},
    {"kind": "tag", "key": "staging", "action": "create"}
  ],
  "errors": [],
  "warnings": []
}
```

